===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} [[at the most]]; maximum.
#: {{ux|en|We will be offered $200 '''max'''.}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} {{clipping of|en|maximum}}.
#: {{ux|en|I could lend you $100, but that's my '''max'''.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} An [[extreme]], a great extent.
#: {{ux|en|He pushed himself to the '''max'''.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|slang}} [[gin|Gin]]. <!--from Latin "maximus"-->
#* {{RQ:Byron Don Juan|passage=Oh! for a glass of '''max'''!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1861|title=The Old Roman Well|page=243
|passage='I remember,' said the pale man, 'the fust night as the Dandy ever came to this crib; he sat at this very table, and drank '''max''' with Charley Chatfield. {{...}}}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|min}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|usually|with ''out''}} To reach the [[limit]]; to reach the [[maximum]].
#: {{ux|en|He [[max out|'''maxed''' out]] his odds of dating Rebecca.}}
#: {{ux|en|She [[max out|'''maxed''' out]] all her [[credit card]]s while she was [[out of work]].}}
#: {{ux|en|My car '''maxes''' at 120 mph.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|especially in present participle}} To [[relax]].

